2. Unified 3D MG dynamics

Same structure, now field‑wise:

\[
\frac{dX}{dt} = F_{\text{MG}}(X) = (\dot{g}, \dot{M})
\]

with:

- \(\dot{g}(\mathbf{x}) = \mathcal{G}(g, M, \nabla g, \nabla M, \text{context})\)  
- \(\dot{M}(\mathbf{x}) = \mathcal{M}(g, M, \nabla g, \nabla M, \text{context})\)

So evolvegeometry and evolvematter now operate on 3D arrays and use spatial derivatives.